{
  "changelog": "lao-huangli v1.0.0\n\n- Initial public release for \u8001\u9ec4\u5386/\u9ec4\u5386/\u62e9\u65e5/\u5b9c\u5fcc/\u51b2\u715e/\u5e72\u652f/\u8282\u6c14\u67e5\u8be2\u4e0e\u8bf4\u660e\u3002\n- Provides a reproducible workflow for calculating calendar fields and deriving almanac recommendations using both astronomical data and documented rulesets.\n- Clear process: standardize input \u2192 exact calendrical/astronomical computation \u2192 rule-based decision engine for \u5b9c\u5fcc and related fields.\n- Distinguishes between precisely computable fields (e.g., lunar calendar, sexagenary cycle, solar terms) and those dependent on traditional rule libraries (e.g., daily recommendations, auspicious/inauspicious designations).\n- Scripts support multiple profiles (market-folk-v1, xiejibianfang-v1, bazi-v1), with factual basis and rule sources clearly labeled.\n- Output format resembles traditional wall almanac, with detailed breakdown and clear marking of calculated fields versus rule-derived results.",
